      "status": "accepted",
      "reason": "A ring homomorphism sends 0_R to 0_S, so the kernel is nonempty; with the established subtraction closure it is an additive subgroup. For arbitrary r in R and x in the kernel, multiplicativity gives phi(rx)=phi(r)phi(x)=0 and phi(xr)=phi(x)phi(r)=0. This proves both absorption conditions and hence the two-sided ideal conclusion without using the theorem as a premise.",
